# GCP deploy — one path only

## Routine (every feature)

```powershell
npm run ship
```

Git push → open PR → auto-merge `main-fixed` → **GitHub Actions** `auto-deploy.yml` → Cloud Run **aibhive** **us-west1**.

No `gcloud builds submit` from the PC. No `npm run deploy:gcp` unless user explicitly says GitHub is down.

## Forbidden for agents (causes hour-long tarball loops)

- `gcloud builds submit` with `.` from Windows
- `npm run deploy:gcp` / `deploy:cloud-run` without `ALLOW_LOCAL_GCP_DEPLOY=1`
- `--async` on local Cloud Build (hides stuck uploads)
- Retrying local deploy when Actions can ship instead

## If user says “deploy to GCP”

1. Commit scoped changes
2. `npm run ship` (or merge to `main-fixed` if already reviewed)
3. Watch https://github.com/codykayak/AiBhive/actions — **Auto-deploy (web + server)**
4. Verify https://aibhive.com/api/health or feature endpoint

## Emergency only

```powershell
$env:ALLOW_LOCAL_GCP_DEPLOY="1"
.\scripts\deploy-cloud-build.ps1
```

Runs `gcp-upload-guard.mjs` first (blocks Gradle/build junk in the tarball).

